# Python Core Conventions

## Type System (PEP 585/604)

- Use built-in generics: `list[str]`, `dict[str, int]`, `tuple[int, ...]` — never `typing.List`, `typing.Dict`
- Use PEP 604 unions: `X | Y`, `X | None` — never `Union[X, Y]`, `Optional[X]`
- Use `Annotated[type, constraint]` for field constraints
- Type hints required on all public functions and class attributes

## Python Version

- Target: Python 3.11.12
- PEP 695 type parameters (`def f[T](x: T) -> T`) require 3.12+ — use `TypeVar` + `Generic` instead
- Use `match/case` for complex conditionals

## Pydantic v2

- Use `field_validator`, `model_validator` — never deprecated `@validator`, `@root_validator`
- Use `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` — never inner `class Config:`
- Apply `strict=True` for business-critical fields
- Use `SecretStr` for sensitive data

## File Operations

- Use `pathlib.Path` — never `os.path`

## Dependency Management

- Always commit `requirements.txt` with pinned versions
- Pin apps with `==`, use ranges (`>=`, `<`) for libraries
- Install: `pip install -r requirements.txt`
